<mxCell id="p1852" value="Top merge of [1, 3, 4] and [1, 2, 5]: the left 1 goes first (ties go left); then the right 1 goes while 3 and 4 remain on the left → +2; then the right 2 → +2 more." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="424" width="820" height="34" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="p1853" value="Total inversions = 6 (1 + 1 + 4 across the merges). Two halves plus a linear merge gives O(N log N). If parts overlap and repeat, use DP." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=13;align=left;spacingLeft=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="464" width="820" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
